% p(Y1, ..., Y8)? reaches p's adornments as tests/lang/magic-budget.dl does,
% but every rule is padded to twenty literals with f literals over
% variables of their own, which bind nothing p is called with.  Each
% adornment copies every rule whole, so the rewrite outgrows its budget of
% generated literals well before its budget of generated rules.  The
% program's size in literals, each body and one for its guard, a fact one,
% is 1 + 21 + 8 x 21 = 190, and its literal budget 256 + 16 x 190 = 3296.
% The warning names the literals, and the query is answered from the whole
% program.

